sting task returns HTTP 200, status `completed`, and a non-empty string `completedAt`.","Reopening that completed task returns HTTP 200, status `pending`, and `completedAt: null`.","The completed/reopened values remain correct when the task is fetched or listed afterward.","Existing task tests continue to pass, including 404 behavior and status filtering."],"verification":["Run the repository test script: `npm test`.","Confirm the existing `complete and reopen` tests pass; they directly assert the required timestamp and clearing behavior.","Optionally add or retain service-level/API assertions that a task fetched after completion has the timestamp and after reopening has `null`, then rerun `npm test`."],"ambiguities":[{"question":"What timestamp representation should be used?","classification":"safe_inference","status":"resolved","resolution":"Use a non-empty ISO 8601 timestamp string generated at completion, such as `new Date().toISOString()`.","basis":"The task requires a timestamp, `Task.completedAt` is typed as `string | null`, and the existing tests require only a non-empty string; ISO 8601 is the standard low-risk representation."},{"question":"Should repeated completion of an already completed task preserve or replace its timestamp?","classification":"safe_inference","status":"resolved","resolution":"The required contract applies when completion is performed; assigning a fresh timestamp on each successful complete operation is acceptable unless the implementation chooses to preserve an existing timestamp. No test or repository contract specifies repeated-completion timestamp identity.","basis":"The task and tests specify the transition to completed and reopening, but provide no repeated-completion identity requirement; this is a local implementation detail outside the requested behavior."}]},"specPath":"/Users/i.kohanvs/Desktop/ai-native/traces/CHK01-interrupted-2026-09-16T21-16-43-968Z-B.spec.json","implementationStarted":false,"failureReason":null,"unresolv